From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 07:45:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/23] Harness: production bounded holders in run.py,
 stable-heartbeat wait, entity vocabulary format fix; reviews of 1b74545

run.py --max-open-holders uses the product's EmbeddedHolders bound (dormant holders woken by their
inbox) instead of harness-level laziness, and waits for two identical heartbeat snapshots before the
first wave. The public entity list now uses the options' form (the plain-string form made the scorer
count every entity twice and zeroed every positive class in C1). Reviews: scale repairs accepted;
term index blocked on B1 (publication must follow the effective ACL).

